## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical, auditable CAPA design for IaC drift and nonconforming changes in a multi-tenant setup, plus concrete API, lifecycle, and metrics.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model
- Lifecycle state machine
- Evidence capture and auditability
- IaC drift detection and canary remediation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal API sketch for POST /caps
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  // store CAPA with req.body evidence
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'CAPA-123', ...req.body });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for audit logging and compliance needs?
- How would you prioritize CAPAs with conflicting remediation actions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design CAPA from data governance, not just incident response.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model for evidence, artifacts, and policy checks
- Lifecycle state machine with DETECT → INVESTIGATE → CONTAIN → REMEDIATE → VERIFY → CLOSED
- Minimal REST API design for CAPA creation/update with linked traces
- Region-aware compliance metrics (violation rate, MTTR, FP rate)
- RCA template and canary rollout with automated data redaction

## Code Example
```javascript
// CAPA data model sketch (TypeScript)
type CAPARecord = {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  evidenceUrls: string[];
  policyChecks: string[];
  region: string;
  state: 'DETECTED'|'INVESTIGATING'|'CONTAINED'|'REMEDIATED'|'VERIFIED'|'CLOSED';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you surface policy checks in runtime dashboards?
- How would you automate data redaction in canary tests before broader rollout?
